   "text": "I read the structure in sections and assembled the SMILES in the same order.\n\n**Left to right**\n- **Pyridazine:** it carries an NH2 and a 2-hydroxyphenyl group. The ring nitrogen of the bicycle is attached next to the NH2.\n- **Bicycle:** the bridged system has bridgehead carbons, a one-atom N bridge, a two-carbon bridge and a CH2\u2013N\u2013CH2 bridge. That makes it a 3,8-diazabicyclo[3.2.1]octane. The N of the CH2\u2013N\u2013CH2 bridge bonds to the pyridazine, and the one-atom N bridge bonds to the pyridine.\n- **Pyridine:** it is substituted at C4 by the bicycle N and at C2 by an O linking to the cyclobutane.\n- **Cyclobutane:** it is 1,3-disubstituted with a wedged O (to pyridine) and a hashed O (to piperidine). I assigned the stereodescriptors from the wedge/hash geometry.\n- **Piperidines:** a piperidin-4-yl ether is joined through N\u2013CH2 to a second piperidin-4-yl. The second piperidine's N is attached to C3 of an isoxazole.\n- **Isoxazole side chain:** C5 of the isoxazole carries a CH(iPr) stereocentre, drawn with a wedge, followed by C(=O).\n- **Hydroxyproline:** an amide to a 4-hydroxypyrrolidine with 2S,4R-type stereochemistry (hashed OH, wedged carboxamide at C2).\n- **Aryl amide end:** the amide N is bonded to a CH(CH3) with a wedged methyl. This carbon bears an aryl ring that has a meta NH2 and, para to the CH carbon, a 4-methylthiazol-5-yl group.\n\nI checked the ring closures and branch parentheses by hand, but I did not run the SMILES through a parser.\n\nSMILES: Nc1nnc(-c2ccccc2O)cc1N1CC2CCC(C1)N2c1ccnc(O[C@H]3C[C@H](OC4CCN(CC5CCN(c6cc([C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N7C[C@H](O)C[C@H]7C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c7cc(N)c(-c8scnc8C)cc7)on6)CC5)CC4)C3)c1"
  }
